2025-06-18 20:12:24,638 - INFO - logger_config.logger_config - Agent responded with message: content="Here's a recipe for Mexican Tacos with Homemade Salsa:\n\n## Authentic Mexican Tacos with Homemade Salsa\n\nThis recipe focuses on simple, flavorful ingredients and techniques to achieve authentic Mexican taco flavors.\n\n**Yields:** About 8-10 tacos\n**Prep time:** 30 minutes\n**Cook time:** 30-45 minutes\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n**For the Meat (Carne Asada - Grilled Beef):**\n\n*   1.5 - 2 lbs Flank Steak or Skirt Steak\n*   1/4 cup Orange Juice\n*   1/4 cup Lime Juice\n*   2 cloves Garlic, minced\n*   1 tbsp Olive Oil\n*   1 tbsp Soy Sauce (optional, for extra umami)\n*   1 tsp Cumin\n*   1 tsp Chili Powder\n*   1/2 tsp Dried Oregano\n*   1/4 tsp Black Pepper\n*   Salt to taste\n\n**For the Salsa (Pico de Gallo):**\n\n*   2-3 Roma Tomatoes, diced\n*   1/2 White Onion, finely diced\n*   1-2 Jalapeños, seeded and finely diced (adjust to your spice preference)\n*   1/4 cup Cilantro, chopped\n*   2 tbsp Lime Juice\n*   Salt to taste\n\n**For the Tacos:**\n\n*   8-10 Corn Tortillas (small, street-style tortillas are best)\n*   Optional Toppings:\n    *   Lime wedges\n    *   Chopped White Onion\n    *   Cilantro\n    *   Radishes, thinly sliced\n    *   Queso Fresco, crumbled\n\n**Equipment:**\n\n*   Large bowl or ziplock bag\n*   Grill or cast iron skillet\n*   Cutting board\n*   Knife\n*   Small bowl\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n**1. Marinate the Meat:**\n\n*   In a large bowl or ziplock bag, combine the orange juice, lime juice, minced garlic, olive oil, soy sauce (if using), cumin, chili powder, oregano, black pepper, and salt.\n*   Add the flank or skirt steak to the marinade, ensuring it's fully coated.\n*   Marinate for at least 30 minutes, or up to 4 hours in the refrigerator. The longer it marinates, the more flavorful and tender it will be.\n\n**2. Prepare the Salsa (Pico de Gallo):**\n\n*   In a small bowl, combine the diced tomatoes, diced onion, diced jalapeño (if using), chopped cilantro, and lime juice.\n*   Season with salt to taste.\n*   Stir well and set aside. The flavors will meld together as it sits.\n\n**3. Cook the Meat:**\n\n*   Preheat your grill to high heat or a cast iron skillet over medium-high heat.\n*   Remove the steak from the marinade and pat it dry with paper towels. This will help it sear properly.\n*   Grill or sear the steak for 3-5 minutes per side for medium-rare, or longer depending on your desired level of doneness. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature: 130-135°F for medium-rare, 135-145°F for medium.\n*   Once cooked, remove the steak from the grill or skillet and let it rest for at least 10 minutes before slicing. This allows the juices to redistribute, resulting in a more tender and flavorful steak.\n\n**4. Warm the Tortillas:**\n\n*   While the steak is resting, warm the corn tortillas. You can do this in a dry skillet over medium heat, on a comal (if you have one), or wrapped in a damp paper towel and microwaved for 30 seconds to 1 minute. The goal is to make them pliable and warm.\n\n**5. Slice and Assemble the Tacos:**\n\n*   Thinly slice the steak against the grain. This will ensure it's tender and easy to chew.\n*   Fill each warm tortilla with the sliced steak.\n*   Top with the prepared salsa (Pico de Gallo).\n*   Add any optional toppings you desire, such as lime wedges, chopped onion, cilantro, radishes, or queso fresco.\n\n**6. Serve and Enjoy!**\n\n**Tips and Variations:**\n\n*   **Meat Alternatives:** You can substitute the beef with chicken, pork, or even mushrooms for a vegetarian option. Adjust the marinade and cooking times accordingly.\n*   **Salsa Variations:** Experiment with different types of salsa, such as salsa verde (green salsa) or a roasted tomato salsa.\n*   **Spice Level:** Adjust the amount of jalapeño in the salsa to control the heat. You can also use other types of peppers, such as serrano peppers, for a different flavor profile.\n*   **Tortilla Options:** While corn tortillas are traditional, you can also use flour tortillas if you prefer.\n*   **Marinating Time:** While 30 minutes is the minimum, marinating the steak overnight will result in a more flavorful and tender result.\n*   **Grilling Tips:** If using a charcoal grill, use hardwood lump charcoal for the best flavor.\n*   **Restaurant Style:** For that authentic restaurant taco experience, try lightly charring the tortillas on the grill after warming them.\n\nEnjoy your delicious homemade Mexican tacos! Buen provecho!" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []} name='You are llm expert' id='run-5afeda91-fdb9-4e10-b2f3-d5cd49c91d30-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1713, 'output_tokens': 1125, 'total_tokens': 2838, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}
2025-06-18 20:12:24,640 - INFO - logger_config.logger_config - Recipe agent result: content="Here's a recipe for Mexican Tacos with Homemade Salsa:\n\n## Authentic Mexican Tacos with Homemade Salsa\n\nThis recipe focuses on simple, flavorful ingredients and techniques to achieve authentic Mexican taco flavors.\n\n**Yields:** About 8-10 tacos\n**Prep time:** 30 minutes\n**Cook time:** 30-45 minutes\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n**For the Meat (Carne Asada - Grilled Beef):**\n\n*   1.5 - 2 lbs Flank Steak or Skirt Steak\n*   1/4 cup Orange Juice\n*   1/4 cup Lime Juice\n*   2 cloves Garlic, minced\n*   1 tbsp Olive Oil\n*   1 tbsp Soy Sauce (optional, for extra umami)\n*   1 tsp Cumin\n*   1 tsp Chili Powder\n*   1/2 tsp Dried Oregano\n*   1/4 tsp Black Pepper\n*   Salt to taste\n\n**For the Salsa (Pico de Gallo):**\n\n*   2-3 Roma Tomatoes, diced\n*   1/2 White Onion, finely diced\n*   1-2 Jalapeños, seeded and finely diced (adjust to your spice preference)\n*   1/4 cup Cilantro, chopped\n*   2 tbsp Lime Juice\n*   Salt to taste\n\n**For the Tacos:**\n\n*   8-10 Corn Tortillas (small, street-style tortillas are best)\n*   Optional Toppings:\n    *   Lime wedges\n    *   Chopped White Onion\n    *   Cilantro\n    *   Radishes, thinly sliced\n    *   Queso Fresco, crumbled\n\n**Equipment:**\n\n*   Large bowl or ziplock bag\n*   Grill or cast iron skillet\n*   Cutting board\n*   Knife\n*   Small bowl\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n**1. Marinate the Meat:**\n\n*   In a large bowl or ziplock bag, combine the orange juice, lime juice, minced garlic, olive oil, soy sauce (if using), cumin, chili powder, oregano, black pepper, and salt.\n*   Add the flank or skirt steak to the marinade, ensuring it's fully coated.\n*   Marinate for at least 30 minutes, or up to 4 hours in the refrigerator. The longer it marinates, the more flavorful and tender it will be.\n\n**2. Prepare the Salsa (Pico de Gallo):**\n\n*   In a small bowl, combine the diced tomatoes, diced onion, diced jalapeño (if using), chopped cilantro, and lime juice.\n*   Season with salt to taste.\n*   Stir well and set aside. The flavors will meld together as it sits.\n\n**3. Cook the Meat:**\n\n*   Preheat your grill to high heat or a cast iron skillet over medium-high heat.\n*   Remove the steak from the marinade and pat it dry with paper towels. This will help it sear properly.\n*   Grill or sear the steak for 3-5 minutes per side for medium-rare, or longer depending on your desired level of doneness. Use a meat thermometer to check the internal temperature: 130-135°F for medium-rare, 135-145°F for medium.\n*   Once cooked, remove the steak from the grill or skillet and let it rest for at least 10 minutes before slicing. This allows the juices to redistribute, resulting in a more tender and flavorful steak.\n\n**4. Warm the Tortillas:**\n\n*   While the steak is resting, warm the corn tortillas. You can do this in a dry skillet over medium heat, on a comal (if you have one), or wrapped in a damp paper towel and microwaved for 30 seconds to 1 minute. The goal is to make them pliable and warm.\n\n**5. Slice and Assemble the Tacos:**\n\n*   Thinly slice the steak against the grain. This will ensure it's tender and easy to chew.\n*   Fill each warm tortilla with the sliced steak.\n*   Top with the prepared salsa (Pico de Gallo).\n*   Add any optional toppings you desire, such as lime wedges, chopped onion, cilantro, radishes, or queso fresco.\n\n**6. Serve and Enjoy!**\n\n**Tips and Variations:**\n\n*   **Meat Alternatives:** You can substitute the beef with chicken, pork, or even mushrooms for a vegetarian option. Adjust the marinade and cooking times accordingly.\n*   **Salsa Variations:** Experiment with different types of salsa, such as salsa verde (green salsa) or a roasted tomato salsa.\n*   **Spice Level:** Adjust the amount of jalapeño in the salsa to control the heat. You can also use other types of peppers, such as serrano peppers, for a different flavor profile.\n*   **Tortilla Options:** While corn tortillas are traditional, you can also use flour tortillas if you prefer.\n*   **Marinating Time:** While 30 minutes is the minimum, marinating the steak overnight will result in a more flavorful and tender result.\n*   **Grilling Tips:** If using a charcoal grill, use hardwood lump charcoal for the best flavor.\n*   **Restaurant Style:** For that authentic restaurant taco experience, try lightly charring the tortillas on the grill after warming them.\n\nEnjoy your delicious homemade Mexican tacos! Buen provecho!" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []} name='You are llm expert' id='run-5afeda91-fdb9-4e10-b2f3-d5cd49c91d30-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1713, 'output_tokens': 1125, 'total_tokens': 2838, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}
2025-06-19 11:29:28,870 - INFO - logger_config.logger_config - Calling general agent with state: {'messages': [HumanMessage(content='what is AI in space.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='8bd77d76-1141-476b-91cf-f812c3514707'), AIMessage(content="I need more information to answer your question effectively. Could you please provide some examples of what you'd like to know about AI in space?", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []}, name='You are llm expert', id='run-69c262d4-511e-4add-a651-9e7b74c624d9-0', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 299, 'output_tokens': 30, 'total_tokens': 329, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}), AIMessage(content=['Could you please specify what you would like to know about AI in space? For example, are you interested in its applications, benefits, or challenges?'], additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='d40fbcb3-3505-484f-9dea-57e8191da01d'), HumanMessage(content='what is machine learning ', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0b20fc2b-9987-436b-b534-e3a7eb79514c'), AIMessage(content='There are many types of machine learning, including:\n\n1.  **Supervised Learning**: The algorithm is trained on labeled data.\n2.  **Unsupervised Learning**: The algorithm is trained on unlabeled data.\n3.  **Reinforcement Learning**: The algorithm learns by interacting with an environment and receiving rewards or penalties.\n4.  **Semi-supervised Learning**: The algorithm is trained on a combination of labeled and unlabeled data.\n5.  **Self-supervised Learning**: The algorithm generates its own labels or targets from unlabeled data.\n6.  **Deep Learning**: Uses neural networks with multiple layers.\n7.  **Transfer Learning**: A pre-trained model is fine-tuned on a new task.\n8.  **Online Learning**: The algorithm is trained incrementally with new data arriving continuously.\n9.  **Active Learning**: The algorithm selects which data points to label next.\n10. **Explainable Machine Learning**: Focuses on understanding the decisions made by a model.\n11. **Robot Learning**: The algorithm learns to control a physical robot.\n12. **Meta-Learning**: The algorithm learns to learn from a variety of tasks.\n13. **Multimodal Learning**: The algorithm learns to recognize and process multiple types of data.\n14. **Cognitive Architectures**: The algorithm is designed to mimic the structure and function of the human brain.\n15. **Evolutionary Computation**: The algorithm uses evolutionary principles to search for good solutions.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []}, name='You are llm expert', id='run-a048c74d-d3db-410b-b926-943986772d00-0', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1804, 'output_tokens': 315, 'total_tokens': 2119, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}), HumanMessage(content='my name is prit', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='f97837cf-b6e7-4826-a460-162ca7a69f79'), HumanMessage(content='What is AI', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='7df502c3-b94e-4626-801b-e17a7ad7849a'), AIMessage(content='AI has numerous applications across various industries, including healthcare (medical diagnosis, personalized medicine), education (personalized learning, intelligent tutoring), finance (risk management, portfolio management), customer service (chatbots, sentiment analysis), transportation (self-driving cars, route optimization), manufacturing (predictive maintenance, quality control), cybersecurity (threat detection, incident response), marketing (predictive analytics, personalized marketing), home automation (smart homes, energy efficiency), and environmental conservation (climate modeling, conservation efforts).', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []}, name='You are llm expert', id='run-87a73d16-5e32-447f-ac43-236d724216de-0', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2126, 'output_tokens': 98, 'total_tokens': 2224, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}), HumanMessage(content='What is AI', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='fcf1af3e-a95a-4a27-bd61-37008e260dfd'), AIMessage(content="AI, or Artificial Intelligence, is a broad field of computer science focused on designing and developing intelligent agents. These agents are systems that can reason, learn, and act autonomously to achieve specific goals. It's a multidisciplinary field involving computer science, mathematics, philosophy, and cognitive science.", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []}, name='You are llm expert', id='run-64aaf373-6fd1-43a0-a2e4-8c55f897d477-0', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1938, 'output_tokens': 60, 'total_tokens': 1998, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}), HumanMessage(content='what is AI', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='fd918c28-d621-461d-bb98-52829cf7dedd'), AIMessage(content="Could you please provide more details or context about what specifically you'd like to know about AI?", additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []}, name='You are llm expert', id='run-89680686-99a2-4525-b613-2fc3d4535781-0', usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 879, 'output_tokens': 21, 'total_tokens': 900, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}), HumanMessage(content='My name is prit', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='c0ac2497-ccd8-4de4-b4e1-1981071aeb9d'), HumanMessage(content='my name is prit', additional_kwargs=