2025-06-19 16:29:37,158 - INFO - logger_config.logger_config - Agent responded with message: content="Here is a recipe for Sichuan Hot Pot, Prit.\n\n## Authentic Sichuan Hot Pot Recipe\n\nThis recipe focuses on creating a flavorful and authentic Sichuan hot pot broth. Feel free to adjust the ingredients based on your spice preference and availability.\n\n**Yields:** 4-6 servings\n**Prep time:** 30 minutes\n**Cook time:** 1 hour (for broth simmering)\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n**For the Broth:**\n\n*   **Beef Bone Broth Base:**\n    *   2 lbs beef bones (marrow bones and knuckle bones are best)\n    *   1 gallon water\n    *   2-inch piece of ginger, smashed\n    *   2 scallions, green parts only, bruised\n    *   1 tbsp cooking wine (Shaoxing wine preferred)\n\n*   **Sichuan Hot Pot Broth Ingredients:**\n    *   1/4 cup Sichuan peppercorns (green and red)\n    *   1/4 cup dried red chili peppers (facing heaven or arbol), cut into 1-inch pieces\n    *   1/4 cup fermented black beans (douchi), rinsed\n    *   2 tbsp chili bean paste (doubanjiang), preferably Pixian brand\n    *   2 tbsp chili oil (can use homemade or store-bought)\n    *   1 tbsp cooking wine (Shaoxing wine preferred)\n    *   2-inch piece of ginger, sliced\n    *   4 cloves garlic, smashed\n    *   2 star anise\n    *   1 cinnamon stick (2-3 inches)\n    *   2 bay leaves\n    *   3-4 dried shiitake mushrooms, soaked in warm water until softened, then sliced\n    *   1/4 cup rock sugar (optional, for sweetness)\n    *   Salt to taste\n    *   MSG (optional, but authentic)\n\n**For Dipping:**\n\n*   **Protein:**\n    *   Thinly sliced beef (ribeye, sirloin)\n    *   Thinly sliced lamb\n    *   Seafood (shrimp, fish fillets, squid)\n    *   Beef tripe\n    *   Pork belly\n    *   Meatballs\n*   **Vegetables:**\n    *   Napa cabbage\n    *   Spinach\n    *   Enoki mushrooms\n    *   Shiitake mushrooms\n    *   Wood ear mushrooms\n    *   Tofu (firm, soft, fried)\n    *   Lotus root\n    *   Potatoes\n    *   Sweet potatoes\n    *   Winter melon\n    *   Bean sprouts\n*   **Noodles & Starches:**\n    *   Glass noodles\n    *   Udon noodles\n    *   Rice cakes\n    *   Sweet potato noodles\n*   **Dipping Sauces (suggestions):**\n    *   Sesame oil with garlic and cilantro\n    *   Soy sauce with chili oil and vinegar\n    *   Peanut sauce with chili oil and sesame paste\n    *   Hoisin sauce\n    *   Fermented tofu sauce (stinky tofu sauce)\n    *   Chopped cilantro, scallions, garlic\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n**1. Prepare the Beef Bone Broth (essential for depth of flavor):**\n\n*   **Blanch the bones:** Place beef bones in a large pot and cover with cold water. Bring to a boil, then boil for 5-10 minutes to remove impurities. Drain the bones and rinse thoroughly.\n*   **Simmer the broth:** Return the blanched bones to the pot and add the fresh water (1 gallon). Add smashed ginger, bruised scallions, and cooking wine. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to a very low simmer. Simmer for at least 2-3 hours, or even longer for a richer flavor. Skim off any foam that rises to the surface.\n*   **Strain the broth:** Strain the broth through a fine-mesh sieve lined with cheesecloth. Discard the bones, ginger, and scallions. Set the broth aside. This broth can be made ahead of time and refrigerated for a few days or frozen.\n\n**2. Prepare the Sichuan Hot Pot Broth:**\n\n*   **Toast the Spices:** In a dry wok or large skillet over medium heat, toast the Sichuan peppercorns and dried chili peppers for 2-3 minutes, or until fragrant. Be careful not to burn them. Remove from heat and set aside.\n*   **Sauté the Aromatics:** In the same wok or pot, heat the chili oil over medium heat. Add the ginger, garlic, and fermented black beans. Sauté for 1-2 minutes, until fragrant.\n*   **Add the Doubanjiang:** Add the chili bean paste (doubanjiang) and cook for another 1-2 minutes, stirring constantly, until the oil turns red and fragrant.\n*   **Combine with Broth:** Pour the beef bone broth into the pot with the sautéed aromatics and doubanjiang. Add the toasted Sichuan peppercorns and chili peppers, star anise, cinnamon stick, bay leaves, and shiitake mushrooms. Add the cooking wine and rock sugar (if using).\n*   **Simmer:** Bring the broth to a simmer, then reduce heat to low and simmer for at least 30 minutes, or up to an hour, to allow the flavors to meld. Taste and adjust seasoning with salt and MSG (if using). You can also add more chili oil or chili peppers for extra heat.\n\n**3. Prepare the Dipping Ingredients:**\n\n*   Wash and prepare all the dipping ingredients. Slice the meats thinly, arrange the vegetables on platters, and soak the noodles according to package directions.\n*   Prepare your desired dipping sauces.\n\n**4. Set Up and Enjoy:**\n\n*   Pour the hot pot broth into a portable electric hot pot, or a pot on a portable butane burner.\n*   Arrange the dipping ingredients around the hot pot.\n*   Bring the broth to a simmer.\n*   Cook the ingredients in the broth, a few at a time, until cooked through. Use chopsticks or a slotted spoon to retrieve the cooked items.\n*   Dip the cooked ingredients into your desired dipping sauces and enjoy!\n*   Continue to add ingredients to the broth and enjoy the hot pot experience.\n\n**Tips and Notes:**\n\n*   **Spice Level:** Adjust the amount of Sichuan peppercorns and chili peppers to your preference. For a milder flavor, remove some of the seeds from the chili peppers.\n*   **Sichuan Peppercorns:** Sichuan peppercorns have a unique numbing sensation called *ma la*. Don't be afraid of it! It's a key element of Sichuan cuisine.\n*   **Doubanjiang:** Pixian doubanjiang is considered the best, but other brands will work.\n*   **Chili Oil:** Homemade chili oil is best for flavor and control over the heat level. You can find recipes online.\n*   **Broth Variations:** You can add other ingredients to the broth, such as jujubes (red dates), goji berries, or Chinese herbs.\n*   **Vegetarian Option:** Substitute a vegetable broth for the beef bone broth and add more mushrooms and tofu for protein.\n*   **Dipping Sauces:** Experiment with different dipping sauce combinations to find your favorites.\n*   **Enjoy the Experience:** Hot pot is a social and interactive meal. Enjoy the process of cooking and sharing with friends and family!\n\nEnjoy your authentic Sichuan hot pot! Let me know if you have any questions." additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'prompt_feedback': {'block_reason': 0, 'safety_ratings': []}, 'finish_reason': 'STOP', 'model_name': 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'safety_ratings': []} name='You are llm expert' id='run-33e4e0b4-1b1b-4b39-9e8a-29362aa77323-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2200, 'output_tokens': 1570, 'total_tokens': 3770, 'input_token_details': {'cache_read': 0}}
